WEBVTT

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:14.245
Hatenkou Yugi

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.556
Tabidachi wa sone totsuzen
The departure always comes unexpectedly

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:22.027
Guzen no yona hitsuzen
It is destined to happen like a coincidence

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:27.829
Mawari dashita unmei ga kishimu
Your evolving fate starts to grind

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.268
Totsuzen no ame ni sozen
Confused by sudden rain

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.706
Furarete zubunure bozen
Stunned by getting rejected and soaked in the rain

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:41.805
Warai tobase michi wa hirakareru
Let’s laugh it off: a new path will open for you

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:45.616
Muimi na koto ni kakusareteru
What’s the most precious thing

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:49.187
Ichiban daiji na mono wa nani
That’s hidden behind meaningless things

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:57.094
Kitto kiseki wa okosu mono waratte
You can make miracles happen, so keep smiling

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:00.596
My Heartbreaking Romance

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:04.836
Hajikeyo omou mama ni
Let’s go wild as you desire

00:01:04.836 --> 00:01:10.138
Omoshiro yukai sore ga kihon
Have a blast and live it up: that’s my style

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.171
Kimi no Heartrending Sorrow
Your Heartrending Sorrow

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.416
Ima wa mada furenai yo
| will leave it alone for now

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:24.879
Mazu wa koko kara hajimeyo
So let’s begin our adventure right here

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:29.992
Am | ever

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:36.701
Hey, Rahzel.

00:01:36.702 --> 00:01:37.498
Hm’?

00:01:38.036 --> 00:01:40.402
Wouldn’t you like to see the world?

00:01:41.974 --> 00:01:42.770
What?

00:01:43.108 --> 00:01:46.100
| think it’d be good for you to go
on a journey and improve yourself.

00:01:48.547 --> 00:01:49.673
Huh?

00:01:52.084 --> 00:01:53.551
Seriously?

00:01:55.587 --> 00:02:01.685
And thanks to my father who ignores my wishes,
| unexpectedly ended up on a journey.

00:02:03.962 --> 00:02:06.362
| never thought | would suddenly lose my home.

00:02:06.932 --> 00:02:10.060
lf | knew it, | would’ve had seconds at breakfast.

00:02:10.769 --> 00:02:12.964
And | should've finished the foods | don’t like.

00:02:16.575 --> 00:02:18.443
Oh well, that’s enough gloomy stuff!

00:02:18.443 --> 00:02:20.678
| shouldn’t be acting like a total mope.

00:02:20.679 --> 00:02:24.274
If that’s the case, | might as well
make the most of the journey.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:26.641
If possible, having a suitable
travel companion would be nice.

00:02:27.185 --> 00:02:29.949
And as | speak, what good timing...

00:02:35.627 --> 00:02:36.828
A hot guy in sight.

00:02:36.828 --> 00:02:37.988
| better approach him.

00:02:38.597 --> 00:02:40.724
Hey, would you like to...

00:02:48.974 --> 00:02:50.339
You're a lifesaver, Missy!

00:02:50.609 --> 00:02:53.100
A handsome young man
holding a gun in broad daylight.

00:02:53.378 --> 00:02:56.245
A silvery white haired man, whose name is Alzeid.

00:02:56.515 --> 00:02:58.983
Um... Are you a robber or something?

00:03:00.619 --> 00:03:02.246
Are you expecting me to deny it?

00:03:02.521 --> 00:03:07.458
Boldly arrogant, outrageously insolent,
with an expression of complete invincibility.

00:03:09.061 --> 00:03:10.358
What do you want?

00:03:13.899 --> 00:03:15.764
What a cheerless look in his eyes.

00:03:17.402 --> 00:03:18.130
Tell you what!

00:03:21.173 --> 00:03:27.806
I’m going to make your damn boring life
more fun and amusing for you!

00:03:30.215 --> 00:03:31.147
Bang!

00:03:41.593 --> 00:03:44.824
Eternal
Light

00:03:45.897 --> 00:03:51.062
So? This is the setting for the
“fun and amusing life” that you picture?

00:03:51.336 --> 00:03:53.668
R-right, exactly.

00:03:56.341 --> 00:03:59.572
| see. Fooling around
with a ghost in the dead of night.

00:03:59.845 --> 00:04:01.947
So amusing. It really is.

00:04:01.947 --> 00:04:04.848
Never mind! If you think it’s lame, just say so.

00:04:05.417 --> 00:04:07.851
By the way, we're here to perform an exorcism.

00:04:08.386 --> 00:04:10.081
Here is our target, Noma-san.

00:04:10.889 --> 00:04:13.483
She looks as though she wouldn’t even harm a fly.

00:04:13.725 --> 00:04:17.991
Rather, she’s the type of person who would help
anyone who is lost in the forest.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:22.427
The reason we must exorcise someone like her is...

00:04:23.201 --> 00:04:25.403
You know, I’m sorry about earlier.

00:04:25.403 --> 00:04:27.371
ll make it up to you by treating you
to whatever you want.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.768
| never realized that this journey
would be so costly.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.072
How do you usually get by, Alzeid?

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:38.781
| target well-off individuals
and corner them in the back alley.

00:04:39.417 --> 00:04:41.851
Talk about a manly way of living.

00:04:42.154 --> 00:04:46.113
Betting in card games also brings in
high income, by cheating.

00:04:46.925 --> 00:04:49.587
You're well past the age
where it’s cute to be an outlaw.

00:04:49.828 --> 00:04:52.524
You expect too much from others.

00:04:52.831 --> 00:04:55.561
My God, he’s a criminal to the core.

00:04:56.268 --> 00:04:58.600
A journey begins with self-financing.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:01.962
Where do | find a job to make a fast buck?

00:05:03.008 --> 00:05:05.602
Daddy, | want to come home already.

00:05:05.844 --> 00:05:06.902
What’s wrong?

00:05:07.345 --> 00:05:09.939
I’m just inquiring about good paying jobs.

00:05:11.082 --> 00:05:12.947
Then, what is that in your hand?

00:05:13.118 --> 00:05:14.983
He handed it to me voluntarily.

00:05:15.453 --> 00:05:17.080
You should give it back.

00:05:18.356 --> 00:05:19.380
Now, tell me...

00:05:19.624 --> 00:05:21.717
where can we find a job to make a quick buck?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.657
Only something worth more
than what’s in your wallet, or else...

00:05:26.331 --> 00:05:29.033
Jeez, he probably isn’t the right person to ask.

00:05:29.034 --> 00:05:31.400
Yes! Yes! | know a well-paying job!

00:05:33.205 --> 00:05:35.707
Try asking the landowner of this town.

00:05:35.707 --> 00:05:39.108
You can even overcharge, and he'll still hire you.

00:05:40.312 --> 00:05:46.114
There’s an evil ghost that dwells at the edge
of this town, and we’re greatly troubled.

00:05:48.019 --> 00:05:50.988
If you can make short work of it,
you will be rewarded.

00:05:51.323 --> 00:05:52.449
We'll take care of it!

00:05:52.791 --> 00:05:54.986
Rest assured, it’s an easy task for us.

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:04.434
| see. Easy task, huh?

00:06:04.703 --> 00:06:07.035
Quiet. Exorcism is beyond my area of expertise.

00:06:07.405 --> 00:06:08.906
What’s your area of expertise, then?

00:06:08.907 --> 00:06:10.169
Problem solving through brute force.

00:06:11.576 --> 00:06:12.338
Hey, you!

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.843
You must pass on immediately
so | can protect my pride.

00:06:16.081 --> 00:06:18.982
Right now, immediately,
as quick as a flash!

00:06:20.852 --> 00:06:22.683
It isn’t working. Can’t she hear me or what?

00:06:22.854 --> 00:06:24.481
That wasn’t very convincing, was it?

00:06:26.758 --> 00:06:29.158
Good grief. | wish you hadn’t come here.

00:06:29.661 --> 00:06:31.891
Oh, | thought you lost your tongue.

00:06:33.899 --> 00:06:40.065
| was hoping you would quietly leave,
but let me tell you how I’m attached to this place.

00:06:40.572 --> 00:06:42.733
| can’t stand old people’s long conversations.

00:06:42.874 --> 00:06:45.308
I’m eternally nineteen.

00:06:46.011 --> 00:06:49.208
This is a story of a frail and beautiful love.

00:06:49.781 --> 00:06:51.783
What do we do? She’s so into it already.

00:06:51.783 --> 00:06:52.807
Just ignore her.

00:06:52.951 --> 00:06:56.648
The man | loved was the heir
to the wealthiest family in this town.

00:06:56.788 --> 00:06:59.090
On the other hand, | was just a poor farmer’s girl.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:00.558
On the other hand, | was just a poor farmer’s girl.
Oh, let me go first.

00:07:00.558 --> 00:07:01.458
What are you going to bet?

00:07:01.459 --> 00:07:02.255
Dinner.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.962
lt was a love between individuals
from two different classes.

00:07:04.963 --> 00:07:06.225
Huh? Why?

00:07:06.598 --> 00:07:07.724
Are you listening?

00:07:07.866 --> 00:07:08.633
Totally.

00:07:08.633 --> 00:07:09.861
Without paying much attention.

00:07:10.435 --> 00:07:11.993
“Let’s take each other’s hands and run away.”

00:07:12.237 --> 00:07:14.262
That’s what he suggested.

00:07:14.873 --> 00:07:17.842
“Eloping...” What a sweet sound it has.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:21.438
We were supposed to meet here
in this forest on the edge of town.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.282
We promised each other
that if we managed to run away,

00:07:24.282 --> 00:07:26.978
we would celebrate our love with fireworks.

00:07:27.585 --> 00:07:34.047
Just imagining that gave me courage, and it didn’t
bother me to wait by myself in this lonely forest.

00:07:34.326 --> 00:07:38.228
But a cruel twist of fate tore us apart.

00:07:38.763 --> 00:07:44.531
While | was waiting for him,
| fell over and died by hitting my head.

00:07:45.003 --> 00:07:45.803
What an idiot.

00:07:45.804 --> 00:07:47.567
I don’t think | can relate to that.

00:07:47.772 --> 00:07:52.209
From then on, I’ve been patiently
waiting here to see him again.

00:07:52.677 --> 00:07:56.238
There you have it.
Now would you leave me in peace?

00:07:59.985 --> 00:08:02.112
So, how long do you intend to wait for him?

00:08:03.455 --> 00:08:07.221
Including the day you promised to meet,
he hasn’t shown up in the past twenty years.

00:08:07.792 --> 00:08:10.420
That’s because | died.

00:08:10.996 --> 00:08:16.992
But still, how come he never left a flower or two,
especially for a woman he loved?

00:08:23.274 --> 00:08:26.334
I’m here to peacefully discuss this.

00:08:26.511 --> 00:08:27.944
Don’t interfere, Alzeid!

00:08:28.446 --> 00:08:33.008
Don’t criticize our love,
and please never come here again.

00:08:33.385 --> 00:08:35.114
| will show no mercy next time.

00:08:37.322 --> 00:08:37.655
Okay—

00:08:37.655 --> 00:08:39.520
You still think you have a next time?

00:08:40.558 --> 00:08:44.995
What do you expect from a man
who couldn’t keep his own word?

00:08:45.263 --> 00:08:46.525
What do | expect?

00:08:46.831 --> 00:08:49.823
Another frail promise that gives
you the pain of betrayal?

00:08:50.201 --> 00:08:52.635
Betrayal? A frail promise?

00:08:52.837 --> 00:08:56.540
Yeah, just like fireworks that vanish in an instant.

00:08:56.541 --> 00:08:58.668
No, he would never betray me!

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.978
| know he’ll keep his word.

00:09:01.212 --> 00:09:02.645
We promised!

00:09:08.686 --> 00:09:09.516
She disappeared.

00:09:10.021 --> 00:09:11.181
You're useless.

00:09:11.656 --> 00:09:13.351
You got paid in advance, right?

00:09:13.658 --> 00:09:14.692
How about we call it quits?

00:09:14.692 --> 00:09:15.624
No!

00:09:15.794 --> 00:09:19.457
She’s a ghost, but all she's doing
is waiting for someone.

00:09:20.265 --> 00:09:22.699
I’m reluctant to exorcise her forcibly.

00:09:24.936 --> 00:09:25.960
Oh yeah!

00:09:26.137 --> 00:09:29.334
Let’s find the man she’s waiting for
and bring him to her.

00:09:29.741 --> 00:09:33.438
Then she won’t have any reason
to be attached to the earthly world.

00:09:34.612 --> 00:09:35.546
All right.

00:09:35.547 --> 00:09:38.616
Here we go, with operation "Messenger of Love!"

00:09:38.616 --> 00:09:39.750
"Messenger of Love"?

00:09:39.751 --> 00:09:41.343
Let’s start with information-gathering.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:44.354
How is this information-gathering?

00:09:44.722 --> 00:09:46.986
If you're hungry, just say so.

00:09:47.125 --> 00:09:51.323
Information will come to you
when you're taking things easy.

00:09:55.233 --> 00:09:57.224
The master wants to see you.

00:09:58.303 --> 00:09:59.235
See?

00:10:00.004 --> 00:10:01.972
Well, | guess it happens.

00:10:02.474 --> 00:10:03.873
Obviously.

00:10:06.177 --> 00:10:09.112
So, how soon can you finish the job?

00:10:09.314 --> 00:10:12.477
Not to worry. The requested task
will be completed shortly...

00:10:12.917 --> 00:10:16.182
but only if we can have your cooperation.

00:10:16.888 --> 00:10:18.549
What do you mean by that?

00:10:18.957 --> 00:10:23.394
You were Noma-san the ghost’s lover, correct?

00:10:25.163 --> 00:10:25.891
How did you know that?

00:10:26.331 --> 00:10:30.631
| mean, Noma-san isn’t
the type of ghost that harms people.

00:10:31.136 --> 00:10:36.301
So | figured that’s the only reason
you’d go out of your way to exorcise her.

00:10:36.841 --> 00:10:38.172
Good point.

00:10:38.409 --> 00:10:44.973
| didn’t expect an outsider
to read my true intentions, but aren’t you clever?

00:10:46.484 --> 00:10:49.146
What happened with her is just a thing of the past.

00:10:49.687 --> 00:10:54.090
| had an obligation to take over
as the head of the family and prosper.

00:10:54.626 --> 00:10:58.460
| couldn’t afford to give that up for just a girl.

00:11:00.198 --> 00:11:02.133
That’s a euphemism.

00:11:02.133 --> 00:11:05.159
You seduced a naive girl...

00:11:05.803 --> 00:11:10.303
but you started feeling uneasy about
your own future so you ended up dumping her.

00:11:11.476 --> 00:11:13.808
Wow, how simple.

00:11:14.012 --> 00:11:17.038
And then, you made a promise
you had no intention of keeping.

00:11:17.248 --> 00:11:19.250
You don’t know what you're talking about!

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:22.845
If you’re going to make excuses,
why don’t you speak to her directly?

00:11:23.054 --> 00:11:25.818
Don't you at least have a sense of guilt?

00:11:27.425 --> 00:11:29.427
Oh, | guess you're scared.

00:11:29.427 --> 00:11:30.451
Shut up!

00:11:31.129 --> 00:11:34.257
You servants simply need
to do whatever your employer orders!

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.424
Not to worry.

00:11:37.602 --> 00:11:42.198
We'll take care of the matter,
and we swear to keep your secret.

00:11:42.607 --> 00:11:44.973
We'll still finish the task that we’re paid to.

00:11:45.376 --> 00:11:47.105
It’s our job.

00:12:01.492 --> 00:12:02.720
You wanted to see us?

00:12:03.528 --> 00:12:04.790
Take care of it.

00:12:06.564 --> 00:12:07.895
Darn it.

00:12:08.066 --> 00:12:12.025
| wish he had canceled our agreement
so we could’ve squeezed a penalty out of him.

00:12:12.337 --> 00:12:17.240
What if she found out about his betrayal?
| wonder what she would do.

00:12:17.875 --> 00:12:20.605
You’re kinda obsessed with that part, huh?

00:12:21.913 --> 00:12:23.005
Well...

00:12:23.615 --> 00:12:25.378
If | were in her shoes, | would kill him.

00:12:26.117 --> 00:12:28.847
| wouldn’t hear his begging or excuses.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:34.881
| would give him all sorts of pain,
and make him regret until the last breath he takes.

00:12:36.294 --> 00:12:37.090
Rahzel...

00:12:38.563 --> 00:12:41.088
have you ever been betrayed?

00:12:41.633 --> 00:12:46.696
Have you ever been abandoned
by someone you trusted, with no explanation?

00:12:54.279 --> 00:12:55.246
No.

00:12:56.781 --> 00:12:57.748
Then...

00:12:59.617 --> 00:13:01.949
...don't say that so casually.

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:02.814
It disgusts me.

00:13:08.559 --> 00:13:11.551
| don’t think that’s a good idea.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:14.561
You might want to listen
to my advice for your own sake.

00:13:17.969 --> 00:13:19.334
It slipped my mind...

00:13:19.771 --> 00:13:22.865
Alzeid is going after his father’s enemy, isn’t he?

00:13:23.441 --> 00:13:25.932
| still don’t know much about him.

00:13:26.277 --> 00:13:28.404
What kind of suffering has he been going through?

00:13:28.646 --> 00:13:31.979
What kind of pain and sorrow?

00:13:32.283 --> 00:13:36.743
Hey, what do you think I'll feel after my death?

00:13:38.489 --> 00:13:42.391
You sound so philosophical all of a sudden.
What happened, Rahzel-chan?

00:13:43.594 --> 00:13:47.121
Did you catch a cold, or are you getting a fever
from thinking too hard?

00:13:47.632 --> 00:13:50.430
Stop talking to me like I’m sick.

00:13:50.802 --> 00:13:53.270
It just crossed my mind, that’s all.

00:13:53.705 --> 00:13:57.436
Do | have anything that
Ill be attached to even after | die?

00:13:58.509 --> 00:13:59.669
| have it.

00:14:01.212 --> 00:14:03.180
That’s you, of course, Rahzel-chan.

00:14:03.181 --> 00:14:06.284
Wow, maybe you can die once to prove it, then.

00:14:06.284 --> 00:14:10.784
Oh c’mon, I'll prove it with my passion,
so you can physically feel it.

00:14:11.456 --> 00:14:16.189
Then I'll respond physically as well, in a violent way.

00:14:17.195 --> 00:14:18.787
Wait, I see...

00:14:19.197 --> 00:14:20.665
| guess that’s the only way.

00:14:20.665 --> 00:14:21.324
Yep.

00:14:21.833 --> 00:14:24.700
No matter how much you contemplate,
you might not always find an answer.

00:14:25.002 --> 00:14:29.132
In that case, you just need
to continue along the path you believe in.

00:14:29.307 --> 00:14:32.140
Then, would you mind running an errand for me?

00:14:32.744 --> 00:14:35.645
| need pretty, colorful ones— lots of them.

00:14:39.817 --> 00:14:42.718
You bet. At your service, Rahzel-chan.

00:14:47.458 --> 00:14:50.188
He’s as hard to read as ever.

00:14:50.928 --> 00:14:55.695
Since he left me like that yesterday,
I’m not sure how to act towards him.

00:14:57.902 --> 00:14:58.936
What’s the matter?

00:14:58.936 --> 00:15:00.103
Aren’t you going to start?

00:15:00.104 --> 00:15:03.039
l-| was just going over my strategy again.

00:15:03.841 --> 00:15:06.243
If all your ideas are this bad,
you may as well not bother.

00:15:06.244 --> 00:15:07.211
You little...

00:15:07.211 --> 00:15:09.475
Just so you know,
I’m not getting involved this time.

00:15:10.748 --> 00:15:13.512
You’re going to make my life
more fun and amusing, right?

00:15:14.452 --> 00:15:16.977
Alrighty. I'll get started, then.

00:15:20.591 --> 00:15:23.924
Wanna play, Ghost Lady?

00:15:24.595 --> 00:15:27.063
Keep it down. | can hear you just fine.

00:15:27.565 --> 00:15:30.329
Besides, | thought | asked you
not to come here again.

00:15:31.302 --> 00:15:35.773
Well, speaking of which, the man
you’ve been waiting for isn’t coming anymore,

00:15:35.773 --> 00:15:37.074
or he isn’t able to come.

00:15:37.074 --> 00:15:39.668
| mean, he already passed away, apparently.

00:15:39.911 --> 00:15:41.902
Why are you lying?

00:15:44.916 --> 00:15:47.749
Wait, did you know everything from the beginning?

00:15:47.952 --> 00:15:50.750
Remember what | said?
| will show no mercy this time.

00:16:04.101 --> 00:16:07.662
| see. So you can do better
than sitting around moping.

00:16:10.107 --> 00:16:14.373
How come you’re not directing that energy
towards something more positive?

00:16:14.579 --> 00:16:16.638
Like beating up that old man.

00:16:20.117 --> 00:16:22.142
Your “positive” is completely twisted.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.748
The audience must sit back and enjoy the show.

00:16:26.157 --> 00:16:28.091
Then you need to stay back, too.

00:16:28.326 --> 00:16:29.927
Why are you getting in my way?

00:16:29.927 --> 00:16:31.588
I’m just patiently waiting.

00:16:32.096 --> 00:16:34.564
Am | not even allowed to dream?

00:16:35.032 --> 00:16:39.332
All | want is to just keep dreaming of him!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.777
You have magical abilities?

00:16:51.916 --> 00:16:53.110
You've never seen it?

00:16:53.351 --> 00:16:56.787
| guess this is as uncommon as seeing a ghost.

00:16:58.055 --> 00:16:59.283
Brace yourself.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:17.200
He’s just a man.
Stop being swayed by him even after your death.

00:17:17.708 --> 00:17:18.675
Just a man?

00:17:18.676 --> 00:17:20.200
Just a man, huh?

00:17:21.312 --> 00:17:23.041
Then, how about you?

00:17:26.884 --> 00:17:29.253
| guess you weren’t so thrilled
to have a non-paying audience.

00:17:29.253 --> 00:17:30.220
Be quiet.

00:17:30.721 --> 00:17:34.987
You say he’s just a man, but you'd kill him
if he betrayed you, wouldn’t you?

00:17:35.226 --> 00:17:36.659
Were you listening in on our conversation?

00:17:36.928 --> 00:17:38.987
He’s just another man like him.

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:41.990
You never know when
he’ll change his mind and leave you.

00:17:42.433 --> 00:17:45.994
So, I’d be happy to finish him off right here.

00:17:47.238 --> 00:17:48.500
Now, what will you do?

00:17:50.241 --> 00:17:52.835
Good. Those two are gone.

00:17:54.045 --> 00:17:58.545
Yes, Sir. Although, our young men
are no longer of any use.

00:17:58.749 --> 00:18:01.718
Not a problem. | can always hire someone else.

00:18:05.389 --> 00:18:07.357
Hey, wake up.

00:18:08.359 --> 00:18:09.293
Good morning.

00:18:09.293 --> 00:18:11.420
What? How did you get out of the forest?

00:18:12.263 --> 00:18:14.527
I’m here to say goodbye for the last time.

00:18:15.466 --> 00:18:18.924
Honestly, | grew tired
of waiting for you out there.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:24.034
Besides, dealing with the people
you send to me is bothersome.

00:18:24.775 --> 00:18:26.443
Wh-what did you do to those two?

00:18:26.444 --> 00:18:29.607
Then again, saying goodbye
for the last time sounds strange.

00:18:30.348 --> 00:18:32.680
We're headed to the same place after all.

00:18:32.817 --> 00:18:33.875
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:18:34.151 --> 00:18:36.415
| set bombs all over this mansion.

00:18:36.821 --> 00:18:39.415
Within just a few minutes, it'll be blown to pieces.

00:18:39.757 --> 00:18:40.553
That can’t be true!

00:18:40.791 --> 00:18:42.224
Someone, help!

00:18:46.397 --> 00:18:48.627
Well, I'll be waiting for you.

00:18:54.805 --> 00:18:56.864
Wait! Don’t leave me!

00:18:57.041 --> 00:18:59.236
Goodbye, my foolish man.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.942
You’re a hopeless fool.

00:19:05.583 --> 00:19:08.074
But it is actually me that has been truly foolish.

00:19:08.352 --> 00:19:09.785
She was right about that.

00:19:10.988 --> 00:19:12.080
You're a fool.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:21.755
| have no idea how you got such a laughable idea,
but there are no promises between Alzeid and lI.

00:19:22.299 --> 00:19:25.097
There’s nothing to break in the first place.

00:19:25.369 --> 00:19:28.702
We don’t even know anything about each other.
We're just keeping company.

00:19:29.473 --> 00:19:34.934
We may be going our separate ways tomorrow,
but that’s no betrayal.

00:19:35.246 --> 00:19:38.306
| know | said that I'd kill a man who betrayed me...

00:19:38.649 --> 00:19:40.810
but that’s my own choice.

00:19:41.352 --> 00:19:43.877
No one should interfere in my business.

00:19:44.722 --> 00:19:46.587
What | have right here is all | need.

00:19:46.824 --> 00:19:48.155
| don’t need any promises.

00:19:49.093 --> 00:19:50.321
Wanna have a party?

00:19:52.396 --> 00:19:54.864
Let’s have a blast for the last time
and make the most of it!

00:20:01.839 --> 00:20:04.672
It’s beautiful. It really is.

00:20:05.142 --> 00:20:07.133
So beautiful that my heart aches.

00:20:07.578 --> 00:20:12.345
| wonder if I’m headed to somewhere
that is filled with this much light.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:15.585
Who knows, but | hope
it's somewhere you feel warmth.

00:20:15.586 --> 00:20:16.450
Yeah.

00:20:16.954 --> 00:20:22.017
Rahzel-san, when I’m reborn,
| think I'll fall in love with someone again.

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:24.189
What if you end up getting betrayed again?

00:20:24.662 --> 00:20:27.995
Even so, that’s how | will live my life.

00:20:29.266 --> 00:20:30.699
| guess that’s what you’re born to do, huh?

00:20:35.673 --> 00:20:38.403
Man, she passed on So easily.

00:20:38.576 --> 00:20:39.941
Indeed.

00:20:41.579 --> 00:20:44.548
And yet, we spent a small fortune.

00:20:44.548 --> 00:20:45.947
See, we're broke.

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:49.908
| blew our entire reward on fireworks.
| didn’t know they cost that much.

00:20:50.087 --> 00:20:51.918
For someone like you, | guess this isn’t too bad.

00:20:53.157 --> 00:20:54.491
But it turned out well, right?

00:20:54.492 --> 00:20:55.151
What a moron.

00:20:55.426 --> 00:20:57.928
Hey, Al-kiddo, don’t be so harsh.

00:20:57.928 --> 00:21:00.463
Besides, | did a good job running errands, too.

00:21:00.464 --> 00:21:01.398
You were late.

00:21:01.398 --> 00:21:04.196
You'd better at least work hard
to make up for your lost time.

00:21:04.468 --> 00:21:05.235
He’s right.

00:21:05.236 --> 00:21:07.966
| bet you got caught up on a pretty lady on the way.

00:21:08.305 --> 00:21:09.439
Oh, c’mon.

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:11.508
| only have eyes for you, Rahzel-chan.

00:21:11.509 --> 00:21:13.807
Would you die and wait for me
in that forest, then?

00:21:19.183 --> 00:21:20.844
Do you want a promise?

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.318
Then, how about this?

00:21:28.259 --> 00:21:33.162
| hope tomorrow and the days after,
we'll have moments filled with joy.

00:21:43.674 --> 00:21:47.344
Tonari no heya kara
As | hear the sound of laughter

00:21:47.344 --> 00:21:50.973
Waraigoe ga suru
Coming from the room next door

00:21:51.148 --> 00:21:58.350
Ussura mezameru asa ga konna ni Itoshii
| slowly wake up to the morning that | adore

00:21:58.722 --> 00:22:05.958
Dokoka de yumemita ichimai no e ni wa
Somewhere | dreamed of a painting

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:13.534
Mou anata no isu wo kakitashita bakari da yo
| just painted a new chair for you

00:22:13.704 --> 00:22:18.204
Kanashii monogatari ga ima
Even if the sorrowful story

00:22:20.644 --> 00:22:29.348
Curtain no mukogawa machibuse shite itemo
Is lying in wait beyond the curtain

00:22:31.355 --> 00:22:38.591
Ashita ni wa mishiranu hito no yoni nattemo
Even if we may feel like strangers tomorrow

00:22:38.863 --> 00:22:45.996
Anata ga koko ni iru tashika na kiseki wo shinjite
| believe in the perfect miracle that you'll still be here

00:22:46.303 --> 00:22:53.641
Sashidasareta te ni wa wakare no yokan mo naku
The hand you reached out shows no sign of parting

00:22:53.978 --> 00:23:01.714
Tada dakishimetakute ima ruisen ga yurunda
As | grow teary-eyed, | just want to hold you now
